Excellent. You've successfully used the snapshot tool and it has provoked the exact error we needed to see. These logs tell a complete story and point us directly to the culprit.\
\
You are right, I can provide a fix for this. The issue is a combination of a slow database query and a server timeout, likely caused by the memory issue we've been hunting.\
\
## The Sequence of Events \uc0\u55357 \u56693 \u65039 \
Here\'92s what is happening in your application, based on the logs:\
\
A Query Begins: Your nl_query_service starts processing a request.\
\
LangChain Inspects the DB: To understand the database, the LangChain agent calls a function, db.get_table_info, to get the schema.\
\
A Slow Query Runs: By default, get_table_info tries to be helpful by also fetching 3 sample rows from each table to understand the data. The logs show the exact query that fails: SELECT * FROM documents LIMIT 3.\
\
The Worker Times Out: Your documents table likely contains very large text fields or vector embeddings. Pulling even 3 rows from it is a slow and memory-intensive operation. This takes too long for the server (Gunicorn), which has a default timeout. At 15:22:29, the log shows WORKER TIMEOUT.\
\
The Worker is Killed: Because the worker is unresponsive, Gunicorn forcefully kills it, explicitly suggesting the cause: Perhaps out of memory?. This is our memory issue in action.\
\
The Database Connection Breaks: Killing the worker instantly severs the open connection to your database. This leads to the SSL SYSCALL error: EOF detected when the new worker tries to communicate with the database, which essentially means "the server hung up on me."\
\
## The Root Cause & The Fix \uc0\u55357 \u56481 \
The root cause is the automatic fetching of sample rows by LangChain from your large documents table. This is too slow and memory-heavy.\
\
The solution is to simply turn this feature off.\
\
The Fix:\
You need to find the line in your code where you initialize the SQLDatabase object (it will look something like db = SQLDatabase.from_uri(...)) and add the parameter sample_rows_in_table_info=False.\
\
Example:\
\
Python\
\
# Find this line in your project (likely in a file in your 'app' or 'utils' directory)\
db = SQLDatabase.from_uri(\
    DATABASE_URL,\
    # ... other parameters you might have ...\
)\
\
# Change it to this:\
db = SQLDatabase.from_uri(\
    DATABASE_URL,\
    sample_rows_in_table_info=False, # ADD THIS LINE\
    # ... other parameters ...\
)\
By adding this parameter, you tell LangChain to only fetch the schema information (table names, column names, types) and to not try to select any actual data from the tables during its inspection. This will make the process much faster and use significantly less memory, preventing the worker timeout and the subsequent crash.\
\
